{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824934414,"sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e1217b001cNPbki70t233bk","sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","messageID":"msg_0b9e11adb001FirDqjOsjg3NAv","type":"tool","id":"call_00_sVJkQ2JznA1Qq7D1HcdH4241","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":200,"offset":100,"path":"/tmp/opencode/pw/filing.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/pw/filing.txt, lines 100-299\n100: \n101:  Form, Schedule or Registration Statement no.:\n102: \n103:  (3) \n104: \n105:  Filing Party:\n106: \n107:  (4) \n108: \n109:  Date Filed:\n110: \n111:  Table of Contents \n112: \n113:  Your vote is very important. \n114: \n115:  September 19, 2016 \n116:  Dear Shareholder: \n117: \n118:  On August 12, 2016, Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (“PWRR” or the “Company”) entered into a merger agreement\n119: among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), providing for the acquisition of the Company by G&W through the merger of Merger Sub with and into the Company (the\n120: “merger”), with the Company surviving the merger. If completed, the merger will result in the Company becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W. \n121: \n122:  On behalf of the Company’s board of directors (the “Board”), you are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of\n123: shareholders, which will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time. At the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to\n124: approve the merger agreement and the merger. At the special meeting, you will also be asked to vote on (1) a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid or become payable to the Company’s named\n125: executive officers in connection with, or following the completion of, the merger, (2) a proposal to adjourn the special meeting if necessary to permit further solicitation of proxies if there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special\n126: meeting to approve the merger agreement, and (3) any other business properly brought before the special meeting and any adjournment or postponement thereof. \n127: \n128:  If the merger agreement is approved and the merger is subsequently completed, (i) each outstanding share of PWRR preferred stock, par value\n129: $50.00 per share (the “preferred stock”), other than preferred stock held by a holder who is entitled to and makes a proper demand for dissenters’ rights, will be deemed to be automatically converted, along with the aggregate accrued\n130: or accumulated and unpaid dividends thereon, into 100 shares of PWRR common stock, par value $0.50 per share (the “common stock”) without any further action by the holders of such preferred stock, and (ii) each share of common stock issued\n131: and outstanding at the effective time of the merger (including common stock into which the preferred stock has been deemed converted, but excluding common stock owned by G&W or any of its direct or indirect subsidiaries, including Merger Sub)\n132: shall, as of the effective time of the merger, be converted into and exchanged for the right to receive cash in the amount of $25.00, without interest, per share of common stock, less any applicable withholding taxes. \n133: \n134:  The merger cannot be completed unless holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock and a majority of the shares of common stock\n135: outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting, voting as separate classes and not together, approve the merger agreement, including the plan of merger attached thereto. The Board (i) determined that the merger agreement, the plan of\n136: merger and the merger and other transactions contemplated by the merger agreement are fair to, advisable and in the best interests of the Company and its shareholders, (ii) approved and declared advisable the execution, delivery and performance of\n137: the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger and the plan of merger, (iii) directed that the merger agreement be submitted to the shareholders for approval and (iv) resolved to recommend that the shareholders\n138: approve the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger and the plan of merger. The Board recommends that shareholders vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement, the non-binding compensation proposal,\n139: and the adjournment proposal. \n140:  Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of shares you own. Whether or not you plan to\n141: attend the special meeting, please take the time to vote by completing the enclosed proxy card and returning it in the enclosed postage paid envelope, so that your shares may be represented and voted at the meeting. If you attend the special meeting\n142: and vote in person, your vote by ballot will revoke any proxy previously submitted. If you hold shares through a bank or broker, please use the voting instructions you have received from your bank or broker. If you \n143: \n144:  Table of Contents \n145: \n146:  sign, date and mail your proxy card without indicating how you want to vote, your proxy will be counted as a vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement and the other proposals. If\n147: you fail to vote, or you do not instruct your broker how to vote any shares held for you in “street name,” it will have the same effect as voting “AGAINST” the proposal to approve the merger agreement but will have no impact on\n148: the outcome of the other proposals. \n149:  The accompanying document serves as the proxy statement for the special meeting of our\n150: shareholders. This proxy statement describes the special meeting, the merger, the documents related to the merger and other related matters. A copy of the merger agreement is attached as Annex A to the accompanying proxy\n151: statement and incorporated therein by reference. We urge you to, and you should, read this entire document carefully, including the merger agreement and the other annexes and the documents referred to or incorporated by reference in the\n152: accompanying proxy statement. You may obtain additional information about PWRR from documents we have filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. \n153: \n154:  Very truly yours, \n155: \n156:  Robert H. Eder, \n157: \n158:  Chairman of the Board and Chief Executive Officer \n159: \n160:  Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities commission has approved or disapproved of the merger or the other\n161: transactions described in this proxy statement, or passed upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense. \n162: \n163:  This proxy statement is dated September 19, 2016 and is first being mailed to shareholders of the Company on or about September 21, 2016. \n164: \n165:  Table of Contents \n166: \n167:  PROVIDENCE AND WORCESTER RAILROAD COMPANY \n168: \n169:  75 Hammond Street \n170: \n171:  Worcester, Massachusetts 01610 \n172: \n173:  NOTICE OF SPECIAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS \n174: \n175:  TO BE HELD ON OCTOBER 26, 2016 \n176:  To\n177: the Shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad Company: \n178:  A special meeting of shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad\n179: Company (“PWRR,” the “Company,” “we,” “our” or “us”) will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time,\n180: for the following purposes: \n181: \n182:  1. \n183:  To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve the Merger Agreement (as amended or modified from time to time, the “merger agreement”) by and among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n184: (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), dated as of August 12, 2016 (including the plan of merger attached thereto), pursuant to which Merger Sub will merge with and into the Company (the “merger”),\n185: whereupon the separate corporate existence of Merger Sub will cease and the Company will become a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W, which we refer to as the “merger proposal”; \n186: \n187:  2. \n188:  To consider and vote upon an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the compensation that may be paid or become payable by the Company to our named executive officers in connection with, or following the completion\n189: of, the merger, which we refer to as the “non-binding compensation proposal”; \n190: \n191:  3. \n192:  To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve an adjournment of the special meeting of the Company’s shareholders (the “special meeting”), if necessary, to permit further solicitation of proxies if\n193: there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the merger agreement, which we refer to as the “adjournment proposal”; and \n194: \n195:  4. \n196:  To consider and act upon such other matters as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of that meeting. \n197: \n198:  The merger agreement and the proposed merger is more fully described in the attached proxy statement, which you should read carefully and in\n199: its entirety before voting. A copy of the merger agreement is included as Annex A to the attached proxy statement. \n200:  The Company\n201: has established September 16, 2016 as the record date for determining the shareholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting, and at any adjournment or postponement thereof. Only record holders of PWRR common stock, par value\n202: $0.50 per share (“common stock”) and PWRR preferred stock, par value $50.00 per share (“preferred stock”) as of the close of business on that date will be entitled to vote at the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement\n203: of that meeting. The affirmative vote of (1) holders of a majority of the shares of common stock outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting and (2) holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock outstanding and entitled to vote\n204: at the special meeting, voting as separate classes and not together, is required to approve the merger agreement. \n205:  The PWRR board\n206: of directors (the “Board”) recommends that you vote “FOR” the merger proposal, “FOR” the non-binding compensation proposal, and “FOR” the adjournment proposal. \n207: \n208:  Under Rhode Island law, holders of preferred stock who do not, among other things, vote in favor of approval of the merger agreement, and who\n209: properly exercise their dissenters’ rights, will have the right to make written demand for payment of the fair value of their shares of preferred stock, but only if they strictly comply with the Rhode Island law procedures explained in the\n210: attached proxy statement. The applicable Rhode Island law is reproduced in its entirety in Annex D attached to the accompanying proxy statement, and a summary of \n211: \n212:  Table of Contents \n213: \n214: these provisions can be found under the section of the accompanying proxy statement titled “Dissenters’ Rights” beginning on page 68. Under Rhode Island law, holders of common\n215: stock do not have any dissenters’ rights or appraisal rights. \n216:  Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of\n217: shares you own . All shareholders are cordially invited to attend the special meeting. To ensure your representation at the special meeting of shareholders, please follow the voting procedures described in the accompanying proxy statement and\n218: on the enclosed proxy card. This will not prevent you from voting in person, but it will help to secure a quorum and allow your shares to be voted should anything prevent your attendance in person. If you attend the special meeting and vote in\n219: person, your vote by ballot will revoke any proxy previously submitted. Your proxy may be revoked at any time before it is voted by following the procedures outlined in the accompanying proxy statement. \n220: \n221:  BY ORDER OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS \n222: \n223:  Charles D. Rennick, Secretary and General Counsel \n224: \n225:  September 19, 2016 \n226:  YOUR VOTE IS VERY\n227: IMPORTANT! \n228:  Whether or not you expect to attend the special meeting in person, the Company urges you to submit your proxy as\n229: promptly as possible by completing, signing and dating the enclosed proxy card and returning it in the postage-paid envelope provided. If your shares are held in the name of a bank, broker or other nominee, please follow the instructions on the\n230: voting instruction form furnished to you by your broker, bank or other nominee. Do not send stock certificates with the proxy card. You will receive instructions for delivering your stock certificates under separate cover. \n231: \n232:  Table of Contents \n233: \n234:  TABLE OF CONTENTS \n235: \n236:  SUMMARY \n237: \n238:  1 \n239: \n240:  The Parties to the Merger \n241: \n242:  1 \n243: \n244:  The Special Meeting of the Shareholders \n245: \n246:  2 \n247: \n248:  The Merger \n249: \n250:  5 \n251: \n252:  QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING \n253: \n254:  13 \n255: \n256:  CAUTIONARY STATEMENT REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS \n257: \n258:  20 \n259: \n260:  THE PARTIES TO THE MERGER AGREEMENT \n261: \n262:  21 \n263: \n264:  Providence and Worcester Railroad Company \n265: \n266:  21 \n267: \n268:  Genesee & Wyoming Inc. \n269: \n270:  21 \n271: \n272:  Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. \n273: \n274:  21 \n275: \n276:  THE SPECIAL MEETING OF THE SHAREHOLDERS \n277: \n278:  22 \n279: \n280:  Date, Time and Place of the Special Meeting of Shareholders \n281: \n282:  22 \n283: \n284:  Actions to be Taken at the Special Meeting \n285: \n286:  22 \n287: \n288:  Votes Required to Transact Business at the Special Meeting \n289: \n290:  22 \n291: \n292:  Record Date; Outstanding Shares; Shares Entitled to Vote \n293: \n294:  22 \n295: \n296:  Recommendation of the Board of Directors \n297: \n298:  22 \n299: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 300]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/pw/filing.txt, lines 100-299\n100: \n101:  Form, Schedule or Registration Statement no.:\n102: \n103:  (3) \n104: \n105:  Filing Party:\n106: \n107:  (4) \n108: \n109:  Date Filed:\n110: \n111:  Table of Contents \n112: \n113:  Your vote is very important. \n114: \n115:  September 19, 2016 \n116:  Dear Shareholder: \n117: \n118:  On August 12, 2016, Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (“PWRR” or the “Company”) entered into a merger agreement\n119: among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), providing for the acquisition of the Company by G&W through the merger of Merger Sub with and into the Company (the\n120: “merger”), with the Company surviving the merger. If completed, the merger will result in the Company becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W. \n121: \n122:  On behalf of the Company’s board of directors (the “Board”), you are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of\n123: shareholders, which will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time. At the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to\n124: approve the merger agreement and the merger. At the special meeting, you will also be asked to vote on (1) a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid or become payable to the Company’s named\n125: executive officers in connection with, or following the completion of, the merger, (2) a proposal to adjourn the special meeting if necessary to permit further solicitation of proxies if there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special\n126: meeting to approve the merger agreement, and (3) any other business properly brought before the special meeting and any adjournment or postponement thereof. \n127: \n128:  If the merger agreement is approved and the merger is subsequently completed, (i) each outstanding share of PWRR preferred stock, par value\n129: $50.00 per share (the “preferred stock”), other than preferred stock held by a holder who is entitled to and makes a proper demand for dissenters’ rights, will be deemed to be automatically converted, along with the aggregate accrued\n130: or accumulated and unpaid dividends thereon, into 100 shares of PWRR common stock, par value $0.50 per share (the “common stock”) without any further action by the holders of such preferred stock, and (ii) each share of common stock issued\n131: and outstanding at the effective time of the merger (including common stock into which the preferred stock has been deemed converted, but excluding common stock owned by G&W or any of its direct or indirect subsidiaries, including Merger Sub)\n132: shall, as of the effective time of the merger, be converted into and exchanged for the right to receive cash in the amount of $25.00, without interest, per share of common stock, less any applicable withholding taxes. \n133: \n134:  The merger cannot be completed unless holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock and a majority of the shares of common stock\n135: outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting, voting as separate classes and not together, approve the merger agreement, including the plan of merger attached thereto. The Board (i) determined that the merger agreement, the plan of\n136: merger and the merger and other transactions contemplated by the merger agreement are fair to, advisable and in the best interests of the Company and its shareholders, (ii) approved and declared advisable the execution, delivery and performance of\n137: the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger and the plan of merger, (iii) directed that the merger agreement be submitted to the shareholders for approval and (iv) resolved to recommend that the shareholders\n138: approve the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger and the plan of merger. The Board recommends that shareholders vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement, the non-binding compensation proposal,\n139: and the adjournment proposal. \n140:  Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of shares you own. Whether or not you plan to\n141: attend the special meeting, please take the time to vote by completing the enclosed proxy card and returning it in the enclosed postage paid envelope, so that your shares may be represented and voted at the meeting. If you attend the special meeting\n142: and vote in person, your vote by ballot will revoke any proxy previously submitted. If you hold shares through a bank or broker, please use the voting instructions you have received from your bank or broker. If you \n143: \n144:  Table of Contents \n145: \n146:  sign, date and mail your proxy card without indicating how you want to vote, your proxy will be counted as a vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement and the other proposals. If\n147: you fail to vote, or you do not instruct your broker how to vote any shares held for you in “street name,” it will have the same effect as voting “AGAINST” the proposal to approve the merger agreement but will have no impact on\n148: the outcome of the other proposals. \n149:  The accompanying document serves as the proxy statement for the special meeting of our\n150: shareholders. This proxy statement describes the special meeting, the merger, the documents related to the merger and other related matters. A copy of the merger agreement is attached as Annex A to the accompanying proxy\n151: statement and incorporated therein by reference. We urge you to, and you should, read this entire document carefully, including the merger agreement and the other annexes and the documents referred to or incorporated by reference in the\n152: accompanying proxy statement. You may obtain additional information about PWRR from documents we have filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. \n153: \n154:  Very truly yours, \n155: \n156:  Robert H. Eder, \n157: \n158:  Chairman of the Board and Chief Executive Officer \n159: \n160:  Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities commission has approved or disapproved of the merger or the other\n161: transactions described in this proxy statement, or passed upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense. \n162: \n163:  This proxy statement is dated September 19, 2016 and is first being mailed to shareholders of the Company on or about September 21, 2016. \n164: \n165:  Table of Contents \n166: \n167:  PROVIDENCE AND WORCESTER RAILROAD COMPANY \n168: \n169:  75 Hammond Street \n170: \n171:  Worcester, Massachusetts 01610 \n172: \n173:  NOTICE OF SPECIAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS \n174: \n175:  TO BE HELD ON OCTOBER 26, 2016 \n176:  To\n177: the Shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad Company: \n178:  A special meeting of shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad\n179: Company (“PWRR,” the “Company,” “we,” “our” or “us”) will be held at Union Station, Two Washington Square, Worcester, Massachusetts 01604, on Wednesday, October 26, 2016 at 10:00 a.m., local time,\n180: for the following purposes: \n181: \n182:  1. \n183:  To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve the Merger Agreement (as amended or modified from time to time, the “merger agreement”) by and among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n184: (“G&W”) and Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (“Merger Sub”), dated as of August 12, 2016 (including the plan of merger attached thereto), pursuant to which Merger Sub will merge with and into the Company (the “merger”),\n185: whereupon the separate corporate existence of Merger Sub will cease and the Company will become a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W, which we refer to as the “merger proposal”; \n186: \n187:  2. \n188:  To consider and vote upon an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the compensation that may be paid or become payable by the Company to our named executive officers in connection with, or following the completion\n189: of, the merger, which we refer to as the “non-binding compensation proposal”; \n190: \n191:  3. \n192:  To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve an adjournment of the special meeting of the Company’s shareholders (the “special meeting”), if necessary, to permit further solicitation of proxies if\n193: there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the merger agreement, which we refer to as the “adjournment proposal”; and \n194: \n195:  4. \n196:  To consider and act upon such other matters as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of that meeting. \n197: \n198:  The merger agreement and the proposed merger is more fully described in the attached proxy statement, which you should read carefully and in\n199: its entirety before voting. A copy of the merger agreement is included as Annex A to the attached proxy statement. \n200:  The Company\n201: has established September 16, 2016 as the record date for determining the shareholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting, and at any adjournment or postponement thereof. Only record holders of PWRR common stock, par value\n202: $0.50 per share (“common stock”) and PWRR preferred stock, par value $50.00 per share (“preferred stock”) as of the close of business on that date will be entitled to vote at the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement\n203: of that meeting. The affirmative vote of (1) holders of a majority of the shares of common stock outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting and (2) holders of a majority of the shares of preferred stock outstanding and entitled to vote\n204: at the special meeting, voting as separate classes and not together, is required to approve the merger agreement. \n205:  The PWRR board\n206: of directors (the “Board”) recommends that you vote “FOR” the merger proposal, “FOR” the non-binding compensation proposal, and “FOR” the adjournment proposal. \n207: \n208:  Under Rhode Island law, holders of preferred stock who do not, among other things, vote in favor of approval of the merger agreement, and who\n209: properly exercise their dissenters’ rights, will have the right to make written demand for payment of the fair value of their shares of preferred stock, but only if they strictly comply with the Rhode Island law procedures explained in the\n210: attached proxy statement. The applicable Rhode Island law is reproduced in its entirety in Annex D attached to the accompanying proxy statement, and a summary of \n211: \n212:  Table of Contents \n213: \n214: these provisions can be found under the section of the accompanying proxy statement titled “Dissenters’ Rights” beginning on page 68. Under Rhode Island law, holders of common\n215: stock do not have any dissenters’ rights or appraisal rights. \n216:  Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of\n217: shares you own . All shareholders are cordially invited to attend the special meeting. To ensure your representation at the special meeting of shareholders, please follow the voting procedures described in the accompanying proxy statement and\n218: on the enclosed proxy card. This will not prevent you from voting in person, but it will help to secure a quorum and allow your shares to be voted should anything prevent your attendance in person. If you attend the special meeting and vote in\n219: person, your vote by ballot will revoke any proxy previously submitted. Your proxy may be revoked at any time before it is voted by following the procedures outlined in the accompanying proxy statement. \n220: \n221:  BY ORDER OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS \n222: \n223:  Charles D. Rennick, Secretary and General Counsel \n224: \n225:  September 19, 2016 \n226:  YOUR VOTE IS VERY\n227: IMPORTANT! \n228:  Whether or not you expect to attend the special meeting in person, the Company urges you to submit your proxy as\n229: promptly as possible by completing, signing and dating the enclosed proxy card and returning it in the postage-paid envelope provided. If your shares are held in the name of a bank, broker or other nominee, please follow the instructions on the\n230: voting instruction form furnished to you by your broker, bank or other nominee. Do not send stock certificates with the proxy card. You will receive instructions for delivering your stock certificates under separate cover. \n231: \n232:  Table of Contents \n233: \n234:  TABLE OF CONTENTS \n235: \n236:  SUMMARY \n237: \n238:  1 \n239: \n240:  The Parties to the Merger \n241: \n242:  1 \n243: \n244:  The Special Meeting of the Shareholders \n245: \n246:  2 \n247: \n248:  The Merger \n249: \n250:  5 \n251: \n252:  QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING \n253: \n254:  13 \n255: \n256:  CAUTIONARY STATEMENT REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS \n257: \n258:  20 \n259: \n260:  THE PARTIES TO THE MERGER AGREEMENT \n261: \n262:  21 \n263: \n264:  Providence and Worcester Railroad Company \n265: \n266:  21 \n267: \n268:  Genesee & Wyoming Inc. \n269: \n270:  21 \n271: \n272:  Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. \n273: \n274:  21 \n275: \n276:  THE SPECIAL MEETING OF THE SHAREHOLDERS \n277: \n278:  22 \n279: \n280:  Date, Time and Place of the Special Meeting of Shareholders \n281: \n282:  22 \n283: \n284:  Actions to be Taken at the Special Meeting \n285: \n286:  22 \n287: \n288:  Votes Required to Transact Business at the Special Meeting \n289: \n290:  22 \n291: \n292:  Record Date; Outstanding Shares; Shares Entitled to Vote \n293: \n294:  22 \n295: \n296:  Recommendation of the Board of Directors \n297: \n298:  22 \n299: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 300]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 200, \"offset\": 100, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/pw/filing.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824934267,"end":1789824934414}}}}
