{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825300619,"sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e6a7600011HnubtDerBkvNj","sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","messageID":"msg_0b9e66f8d0019uCuNJDnvgL6Sa","type":"text","text":"Now let me verify the exact quotes I plan to use against the filing text, so every quotation is exact.","time":{"start":1789825296224,"end":1789825300619}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825300642,"sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e6a7ce0010skWQFutmOveKc","sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","messageID":"msg_0b9e66f8d0019uCuNJDnvgL6Sa","type":"tool","id":"call_00_6HvOBHj3Qdo4uC9EFCip8034","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\ntext = open('filing.txt', encoding='utf-8').read()\nquotes = [\n\"Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed some interest in acquiring equity in the Company\",\n\"the Board appointed a subcommittee of two independent directors, Frank W. Barrett and Richard W. Anderson, to interview potential investment bankers\",\n\"the Board approved the subcommittee\\u2019s recommendation and the Company engaged GHF\",\n\"Representatives of GHF then proposed a process pursuant to which the Company would proceed with discussions with Party A and also solicit interest from other potential third parties\",\n\"representatives of GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) and 18 potential financial buyers\",\n\"Mr. Noreck reported that the Company had also approached two additional Class I railroads to determine their interest in a possible transaction\",\n\"Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements\",\n\"each potential buyer had been advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by May 10, 2016\",\n\"which deadline was subsequently postponed to May 19, 2016 to ensure the potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers\",\n\"the Company received nine written indications of interest (\\u201cIOIs\\u201d) from potential buyers, with offer prices per share ranging from $17.93 to $26.50\",\n\"the Transaction Committee concluded that the two low bidders should be excluded from that process\",\n\"authorized representatives of GHF to schedule in-person management presentations with the remaining seven potential buyers\",\n\"representatives of GHF instructed all potential buyers to submit non-binding letters of intent (\\u201cLOIs\\u201d) by July 20, 2016\",\n\"a potential strategic buyer that had not previously been part of the process (\\u201cParty C\\u201d) approached the Company\\u2019s management and expressed interest in acquiring the Company\",\n\"After executing a confidentiality agreement, Party C was provided the memorandum concerning the Company provided to the other potential buyers\",\n\"Party C submitted an IOI with an offer price per share of $21.00 (implying an equity value of $108 million)\",\n\"Party C was provided access to the internet data site and the Company\\u2019s management held a management presentation with Party C by telephone\",\n\"Party B submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $24.00 per share (subject to an expedited diligence review)\",\n\"G&W submitted an LOI on July 21, 2016 to acquire the Company for a price of $21.15 per share (subject to a three-week exclusive diligence period)\",\n\"G&W submitted a revised LOI, which increased its offer to $22.15 per share (including $21.02 in cash and $1.13 CVR)\",\n\"Party E (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.26 per share\",\n\"Party D (a financial buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $21.00 per share (subject to a four-week diligence period)\",\n\"Party C submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.30 per share (subject to a 30-day diligence period)\",\n\"Party F (a strategic buyer) submitted an LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $19.20 per share (subject to a 30-day due diligence period)\",\n\"One strategic buyer and one financial buyer elected not to submit an LOI\",\n\"the Company should proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B because of the higher offers made by each of G&W and Party B\",\n\"representatives of GHF subsequently contacted the remaining bidders to inform them that they were no longer involved in the process\",\n\"On August 1, 2016, Party D submitted a revised LOI at a price of $24.00 per share\",\n\"Party E submitted a revised LOI, along with financing support, from Party F, at a price of $23.81 per share\",\n\"Party E withdrew its revised proposal on August 2, 2016 (but confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share)\",\n\"Party D declined to shorten its due diligence period and requested that the Company commit that it would not enter into an agreement with another bidder\",\n\"legal counsel for Party B provided a revised draft of the merger agreement\",\n\"the Transaction Committee directed representatives of BMO to inform G&W that the Company intended to enter into a merger agreement with another bidder\",\n\"G&W submitted a revised LOI to acquire the Company for a price of $25.00 per share in cash, which excluded the previously proposed CVR\",\n\"Party B indicated that it would not increase its price\",\n\"the Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement\",\n\"The Company issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction on Monday, August 15, 2016 prior to the opening of trading\",\n\"During that discussion, the Transaction Committee directed the management team and representatives of each of BMO and Hinckley Allen to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B\",\n\"Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016, the Company received nine written indications of interest (\\u201cIOIs\\u201d) from potential buyers\",\n\"In late July 2016, the Company received six LOIs with offer prices per share ranging from $19.20 to $24.00\",\n\"the two low bidders should be excluded from that process\",\n\"G&W also provided a mark-up of the disclosure letter\",\n\"Party B, G&W and another bidder (\\u201cParty D\\u201d) also p