{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825621936,"sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9eb9830001lB09hXGEBL816w","sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","messageID":"msg_0b9eb5d4700183sKh7cqB5dO0k","type":"tool","id":"call_00_jVr3ewji8rxLNW1kzptl0476","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport io\ns = io.open('build.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\ns = s.replace(\n \"\\\"Catch-up access: after its 07/12 IOI, Party C was given internet data-site access and a telephone management presentation; the seven earlier bidders had in-person presentations.\\\"\",\n \"\\\"Provided late entrant Party C internet data-site access and a telephone management presentation after its 07/12 IOI; the seven earlier bidders had in-person presentations.\\\"\")\ns = s.replace(\n \"\\\"Revised LOI at $25.00 all cash, dropping the CVR; markups of merger agreement and voting agreement (disclosure-letter markup later); offer to expire 6:00 p.m. 08/13; no financing condition in the executed agreement.\\\"\",\n \"\\\"revises #31: $25.00 all cash, dropping the CVR; markups of merger agreement and voting agreement (disclosure-letter markup later); offer to expire 6:00 p.m. 08/13; no financing condition in the executed agreement.\\\"\")\nio.open('build.py','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('edited')\nEOF\npython3 build.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Questions']\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print(\"=====\", r[0], \"| words(Q):\", len(r[1].split()), \"| words(A):\", len(r[2].split()))\n    print(r[1]); print(\"REC:\", r[2]); print(\"WHY:\", r[3]); print(\"ROWS:\", r[4]); print(\"CHG:\", r[5]); print(\"RN:\", r[6])\nws = wb['Deal facts']\nprint()\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print(f\"{r[0]!r}  =>  {r[1]!r}\")\nws = wb['Rounds']\nprint()\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print(r)\nEOF"},"output":"edited\nLEDGER ROWS: 48\nAll ledger validation checks passed.\nSaved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx\nSheets: ['Deal ledger', 'Rounds', 'Questions', 'Deal facts']\n===== Q1 | words(Q): 52 | words(A): 57\nIs the round map right: Round 1 outreach + IOIs (week of 03/28–06/01), Round 2 seven advanced to management presentations and diligence with LOIs due 07/20, Round 3 G&W and Party B in confirmatory diligence and definitive negotiation from 07/27? Or did the mid-June LOI instruction open a new round (making four)?\nREC: Keep three rounds. The 05/23–06/01 advancement opened the stage that produced the 07/20 LOIs; mid-June only set that stage's deadline. If a new round opened mid-June, the six LOI bids and the 07/20 deadline move to Round 3 and the finalists to Round 4. Round 1 could alternatively open 03/24 (Committee authorization), moving only that row's date.\nWHY: C8: rounds turn on target-organized transitions. Advancement of seven: p. 29. Mid-June LOI instruction: p. 29. Definitive negotiation: p. 30. Wave: p. 28.\nROWS: #6, #16, #32; LOI bids #23–#31; deadline rows #12, #17, #22; Party C rows #18–#21; Rounds sheet.\nCHG: Round numbers shift for events after mid-June; deadline outcomes reattach; live-bidder counts per round change. No prices, exits or exit reasons change.\nRN: None\n===== Q2 | words(Q): 40 | words(A): 46\nDeadline outcomes: for Round 1's 05/19 IOI deadline, were the nine IOIs (received 05/19–06/01) Late bids accepted, or Enforced if all arrived by 05/19? For Round 2's 07/20 LOI deadline, G&W's one-day-late LOI was considered: Late bids accepted, or Enforced?\nREC: As recorded: Late bids accepted for both. The IOI receipt window runs past 05/19 and the Committee considered the IOIs on 05/23 and 06/01; G&W's 07/21 LOI was taken up and revised on 07/26. If all six LOIs are treated as in-deadline, Round 2 reads Enforced.\nWHY: p. 29: nine IOIs received “Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016”; “G&W submitted an LOI on July 21, 2016”; LOI deadline “by July 20, 2016” (p. 29).\nROWS: #12, #22; bears on #13, #23, #30 and the Rounds sheet 'Deadline outcome'.\nCHG: Whether G&W's first LOI counts as a late bid fixes the Round 2 outcome; Round 1's turns on when the nine IOIs actually arrived (not separately dated).\nRN: None\n===== Q3 | words(Q): 56 | words(A): 45\nConfidentiality counts: the filing states 25 signers (11 strategic + 14 financial), but Party C, 'not previously part of the process', signs in early July, and the Board's reasons say six of the 25 submitted LOIs — the six include Party C. Does the 25 include Party C, and what base should the 16 non-submitters use?\nREC: Use the stated 25 (11+14) for the auction screen and base the 16 non-submitters on 25 − 9 = 16; treat Party C as an additional late signer with the overlap noted. The screen is Met either way; Party A may sit in the 16.\nWHY: p. 28: “Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements”; p. 33: “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements ... and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent”; Party C p. 29; two Class I railroads p. 28.\nROWS: #7, #8, #9, #14, #19; Deal facts auction screen.\nCHG: If Party C sits inside the 25 the residual is 15; if the two Class I railroads also signed the base grows. The screen stays Met under any reading.\nRN: None\n===== Q4 | words(Q): 43 | words(A): 36\nParty B's Bid reaffirmed (#42, $24.00, 08/04): B's latest priced row sits in Round 2 (Not final), and B's counsel returned a revised merger agreement draft the day the Committee decided to complete the agreement with B. Does a C12 late-reconfirmation row apply?\nREC: Yes — the target moved to finalize on B's standing $24.00 (08/04 decision), B's latest priced row sits in a non-final round, and B's counsel returned a draft on 08/04. Price carried from #23; Conditions Light.\nWHY: p. 31: “legal counsel for Party B provided a revised draft of the merger agreement”; p. 31: “to prioritize Party B and proceed to complete the negotiation of the merger agreement with Party B”.\nROWS: #42; Rounds sheet Round 3 'Bids received'.\nCHG: Without it the runner-up has no formal act inside the final round; Round 3 bidders drop to three (G&W, Party D, Party E).\nRN: None\n===== Q5 | words(Q): 47 | words(A): 30\nParty E's second exit: after reverting to its $21.26 proposal on 08/02, E is never mentioned again. Is E out on 08/04 (Dropped by target, inferred — the Committee then directed continuation with only G&W and Party B) or still live until signing (Not selected at signing)?\nREC: Out on 08/04 by inference: the 08/04 direction names the continuing parties without E, the first transition after its reversion. Record Dropped by target, reason Not stated, Inferred = Y.\nWHY: p. 31: Committee directed “to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B”; E last mentioned confirming its proposal on 08/02 (p. 30).\nROWS: #41; Rounds sheet Round 3; live-bidder count at signing.\nCHG: If E stays live to 08/12, live bidders at signing = 3 instead of 2, and E's exit date and reason change.\nRN: None\n===== Q6 | words(Q): 38 | words(A): 32\nPrice bases: the LOI prices “were based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments”, which the Committee said could affect the ultimate price. Are the recorded per-share prices comparable across bidders?\nREC: Record prices as stated (USD per common share, preferred as-converted) and note the basis difference; do not adjust. The finalists were chosen on the stated higher offers, so the filing's ranking stands.\nWHY: p. 30: “the LOI prices were based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments”; valuation basis “100% of the outstanding common stock on a dollar per share basis” (p. 29).\nROWS: #23, #24, #25, #26, #27, #30, #31; Deal facts 'Currency and units'.\nCHG: If bases are treated as materially different, cross-bidder price comparisons weaken, though the target's final choice at $25.00 stands.\nRN: None\n\n'Target'  =>  'Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR), a Rhode Island regional freight railroad; Nasdaq: PWX; Worcester, Massachusetts'\n'Acquirer'  =>  'Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (G&W), a Delaware corporation, through Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (Merger Sub)'\n'Acquirer type'  =>  'Strategic — operating short-line and regional freight railroad operator (G&W owns or leases 121 freight railroads)'\n'Agreed price and consideration'  =>  '$25.00 per share of common stock in cash, without interest; each preferred share converts into 100 common shares (plus accrued dividends) and receives the same $25.00 per share; all-cash'\n'Merger agreement signed'  =>  datetime.datetime(2016, 8, 12, 0, 0)\n'Merger announced'  =>  datetime.datetime(2016, 8, 15, 0, 0)\n'Filing type and date'  =>  'DEFM14A definitive proxy statement, proxy dated September 19, 2016 and first mailed on or about September 21, 2016; special meeting October 26, 2016'\n'Background pages'  =>  '27–32'\n'Initiation (target-led, bidder-led, activist-influenced, mixed or unclear)'  =>  \"Bidder-led — Party A, a Class I rail partner, raised acquisition interest in Q4 2015, prompting the Board's banker interviews and sale process\"\n'Number of processes'  =>  '1'\n'Auction screen (C1)'  =>  'Met — 25 prospective acquirers executed confidentiality agreements (11 strategic, 14 financial); late entrant Party C signed separately; no standstills (Q3)'\n'Whole-company bids (Yes, or No with what was bid for)'  =>  'Yes — IOIs and LOIs sought 100% of the outstanding common stock (per share, preferred as-converted); final bid $25.00 per share in cash'\n'Currency and units of bid prices'  =>  'US dollars; per-share of common stock, assuming conversion of preferred stock (100-for-1); LOI prices rested on different transaction-expense and change-in-control assumptions (Q6)'\n'Target financial advisers'  =>  'Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC (GHF), selected January 2016; business acquired by BMO Capital Markets Corp. on August 1, 2016 — one adviser throughout; BMO rendered the August 12, 2016 fairness opinion'\n'Target legal advisers'  =>  'Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP'\n'Account (five or six plain sentences)'  =>  \"Providence and Worcester (PWRR), a regional freight railroad, began a sale process after Party A, a Class I rail partner, expressed interest in acquiring equity in the fourth quarter of 2015; the Board engaged GHF as financial adviser in January 2016 and on March 14, 2016 approved a strategy combining talks with Party A with a broad solicitation. In the week of March 28, 2016 GHF contacted 29 potential buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial); 25 signed confidentiality agreements, five strategic buyers met management at an April convention, and the Board set a May 10 IOI deadline, postponed to May 19, 2016. Nine non-binding IOIs came in ($17.93–$26.50 per share); the Committee excluded the two low bidders, advanced seven to management presentations and data-site diligence, and sought non-binding LOIs with markups by July 20, 2016. Six LOIs arrived ($19.20–$24.00; G&W's one day late), and on July 27, 2016 the Committee advanced G&W and Party B to confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation, telling Party C, D, E and F they were out; D and E briefly re-engaged in early August, and Party B reaffirmed its $24.00 on August 4. On August 12, 2016 G&W returned with a $25.00 all-cash LOI (no CVR), Party B declined to raise its $24.00, and the Board determined G&W's offer superior and signed the merger agreement; the deal was announced August 15, 2016. G&W is an operating short-line and regional railroad group, and PWRR's preferred stock converts 100-for-1 into the same $25.00 cash consideration.\"\n\n(1, 1, datetime.datetime(2016, 3, 31, 0, 0), 'Transaction Committee authorized outreach; GHF contacted 11 strategic and 18 financial buyers during the week of 03/28', '25 NDA signers: 11 strategic (incl. Party A, Party B, G&W) and 14 financial; 2 further Class I railroads approached', '05/10/2016 → 05/19/2016', 'Late bids accepted (05/19: nine IOIs received 05/19–06/01)', 'Not final', '9 IOI submitters (unnamed; $17.93–$26.50 per share)', 'Seven advanced to presentations; two low bidders excluded; 16 of 25 signers did not submit')\n(1, 2, datetime.datetime(2016, 5, 27, 0, 0), 'Committee advanced seven to management presentations and data-site diligence; non-binding LOIs with markups due 07/20', '8: seven advanced (5 strategic incl. Party B, G&W, Party E, Party F; 2 financial incl. Party D) + late entrant Party C (strategic)', '07/20/2016', \"Late bids accepted (G&W's LOI arrived 07/21 and was considered)\", 'Not final', '6: Party B $24.00; G&W $21.15 → $22.15; Party E $21.26; Party D $21.00; Party C $19.30; Party F $19.20 (1 strategic + 1 financial did not submit)', 'G&W and Party B advanced to definitive stage; Party C, D, E, F told they were out')\n(1, 3, datetime.datetime(2016, 7, 27, 0, 0), 'Committee advanced G&W and Party B to confirmatory due diligence and negotiations on their higher offers', '2: G&W (strategic), Party B (strategic)', 'none stated', 'No deadline stated', 'Inferred final', '4: G&W $25.00 (08/12); Party B $24.00 reaffirmed (08/04); Party D $24.00 (08/01); Party E $23.81 then $21.26 (08/01–02)', 'signing with G&W on 08/12; Party B, Party D and Party E out')\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"edited\nLEDGER ROWS: 48\nAll ledger validation checks passed.\nSaved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx\nSheets: ['Deal ledger', 'Rounds', 'Questions', 'Deal facts']\n===== Q1 | words(Q): 52 | words(A): 57\nIs the round map right: Round 1 outreach + IOIs (week of 03/28–06/01), Round 2 seven advanced to management presentations and diligence with LOIs due 07/20, Round 3 G&W and Party B in confirmatory diligence and definitive negotiation from 07/27? Or did the mid-June LOI instruction open a new round (making four)?\nREC: Keep three rounds. The 05/23–06/01 advancement opened the stage that produced the 07/20 LOIs; mid-June only set that stage's deadline. If a new round opened mid-June, the six LOI bids and the 07/20 deadline move to Round 3 and the finalists to Round 4. Round 1 could alternatively open 03/24 (Committee authorization), moving only that row's date.\nWHY: C8: rounds turn on target-organized transitions. Advancement of seven: p. 29. Mid-June LOI instruction: p. 29. Definitive negotiation: p. 30. Wave: p. 28.\nROWS: #6, #16, #32; LOI bids #23–#31; deadline rows #12, #17, #22; Party C rows #18–#21; Rounds sheet.\nCHG: Round numbers shift for events after mid-June; deadline outcomes reattach; live-bidder counts per round change. No prices, exits or exit reasons change.\nRN: None\n===== Q2 | words(Q): 40 | words(A): 46\nDeadline outcomes: for Round 1's 05/19 IOI deadline, were the nine IOIs (received 05/19–06/01) Late bids accepted, or Enforced if all arrived by 05/19? For Round 2's 07/20 LOI deadline, G&W's one-day-late LOI was considered: Late bids accepted, or Enforced?\nREC: As recorded: Late bids accepted for both. The IOI receipt window runs past 05/19 and the Committee considered the IOIs on 05/23 and 06/01; G&W's 07/21 LOI was taken up and revised on 07/26. If all six LOIs are treated as in-deadline, Round 2 reads Enforced.\nWHY: p. 29: nine IOIs received “Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016”; “G&W submitted an LOI on July 21, 2016”; LOI deadline “by July 20, 2016” (p. 29).\nROWS: #12, #22; bears on #13, #23, #30 and the Rounds sheet 'Deadline outcome'.\nCHG: Whether G&W's first LOI counts as a late bid fixes the Round 2 outcome; Round 1's turns on when the nine IOIs actually arrived (not separately dated).\nRN: None\n===== Q3 | words(Q): 56 | words(A): 45\nConfidentiality counts: the filing states 25 signers (11 strategic + 14 financial), but Party C, 'not previously part of the process', signs in early July, and the Board's reasons say six of the 25 submitted LOIs — the six include Party C. Does the 25 include Party C, and what base should the 16 non-submitters use?\nREC: Use the stated 25 (11+14) for the auction screen and base the 16 non-submitters on 25 − 9 = 16; treat Party C as an additional late signer with the overlap noted. The screen is Met either way; Party A may sit in the 16.\nWHY: p. 28: “Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements”; p. 33: “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements ... and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent”; Party C p. 29; two Class I railroads p. 28.\nROWS: #7, #8, #9, #14, #19; Deal facts auction screen.\nCHG: If Party C sits inside the 25 the residual is 15; if the two Class I railroads also signed the base grows. The screen stays Met under any reading.\nRN: None\n===== Q4 | words(Q): 43 | words(A): 36\nParty B's Bid reaffirmed (#42, $24.00, 08/04): B's latest priced row sits in Round 2 (Not final), and B's counsel returned a revised merger agreement draft the day the Committee decided to complete the agreement with B. Does a C12 late-reconfirmation row apply?\nREC: Yes — the target moved to finalize on B's standing $24.00 (08/04 decision), B's latest priced row sits in a non-final round, and B's counsel returned a draft on 08/04. Price carried from #23; Conditions Light.\nWHY: p. 31: “legal counsel for Party B provided a revised draft of the merger agreement”; p. 31: “to prioritize Party B and proceed to complete the negotiation of the merger agreement with Party B”.\nROWS: #42; Rounds sheet Round 3 'Bids received'.\nCHG: Without it the runner-up has no formal act inside the final round; Round 3 bidders drop to three (G&W, Party D, Party E).\nRN: None\n===== Q5 | words(Q): 47 | words(A): 30\nParty E's second exit: after reverting to its $21.26 proposal on 08/02, E is never mentioned again. Is E out on 08/04 (Dropped by target, inferred — the Committee then directed continuation with only G&W and Party B) or still live until signing (Not selected at signing)?\nREC: Out on 08/04 by inference: the 08/04 direction names the continuing parties without E, the first transition after its reversion. Record Dropped by target, reason Not stated, Inferred = Y.\nWHY: p. 31: Committee directed “to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B”; E last mentioned confirming its proposal on 08/02 (p. 30).\nROWS: #41; Rounds sheet Round 3; live-bidder count at signing.\nCHG: If E stays live to 08/12, live bidders at signing = 3 instead of 2, and E's exit date and reason change.\nRN: None\n===== Q6 | words(Q): 38 | words(A): 32\nPrice bases: the LOI prices “were based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments”, which the Committee said could affect the ultimate price. Are the recorded per-share prices comparable across bidders?\nREC: Record prices as stated (USD per common share, preferred as-converted) and note the basis difference; do not adjust. The finalists were chosen on the stated higher offers, so the filing's ranking stands.\nWHY: p. 30: “the LOI prices were based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments”; valuation basis “100% of the outstanding common stock on a dollar per share basis” (p. 29).\nROWS: #23, #24, #25, #26, #27, #30, #31; Deal facts 'Currency and units'.\nCHG: If bases are treated as materially different, cross-bidder price comparisons weaken, though the target's final choice at $25.00 stands.\nRN: None\n\n'Target'  =>  'Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR), a Rhode Island regional freight railroad; Nasdaq: PWX; Worcester, Massachusetts'\n'Acquirer'  =>  'Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (G&W), a Delaware corporation, through Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (Merger Sub)'\n'Acquirer type'  =>  'Strategic — operating short-line and regional freight railroad operator (G&W owns or leases 121 freight railroads)'\n'Agreed price and consideration'  =>  '$25.00 per share of common stock in cash, without interest; each preferred share converts into 100 common shares (plus accrued dividends) and receives the same $25.00 per share; all-cash'\n'Merger agreement signed'  =>  datetime.datetime(2016, 8, 12, 0, 0)\n'Merger announced'  =>  datetime.datetime(2016, 8, 15, 0, 0)\n'Filing type and date'  =>  'DEFM14A definitive proxy statement, proxy dated September 19, 2016 and first mailed on or about September 21, 2016; special meeting October 26, 2016'\n'Background pages'  =>  '27–32'\n'Initiation (target-led, bidder-led, activist-influenced, mixed or unclear)'  =>  \"Bidder-led — Party A, a Class I rail partner, raised acquisition interest in Q4 2015, prompting the Board's banker interviews and sale process\"\n'Number of processes'  =>  '1'\n'Auction screen (C1)'  =>  'Met — 25 prospective acquirers executed confidentiality agreements (11 strategic, 14 financial); late entrant Party C signed separately; no standstills (Q3)'\n'Whole-company bids (Yes, or No with what was bid for)'  =>  'Yes — IOIs and LOIs sought 100% of the outstanding common stock (per share, preferred as-converted); final bid $25.00 per share in cash'\n'Currency and units of bid prices'  =>  'US dollars; per-share of common stock, assuming conversion of preferred stock (100-for-1); LOI prices rested on different transaction-expense and change-in-control assumptions (Q6)'\n'Target financial advisers'  =>  'Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC (GHF), selected January 2016; business acquired by BMO Capital Markets Corp. on August 1, 2016 — one adviser throughout; BMO rendered the August 12, 2016 fairness opinion'\n'Target legal advisers'  =>  'Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP'\n'Account (five or six plain sentences)'  =>  \"Providence and Worcester (PWRR), a regional freight railroad, began a sale process after Party A, a Class I rail partner, expressed interest in acquiring equity in the fourth quarter of 2015; the Board engaged GHF as financial adviser in January 2016 and on March 14, 2016 approved a strategy combining talks with Party A with a broad solicitation. In the week of March 28, 2016 GHF contacted 29 potential buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial); 25 signed confidentiality agreements, five strategic buyers met management at an April convention, and the Board set a May 10 IOI deadline, postponed to May 19, 2016. Nine non-binding IOIs came in ($17.93–$26.50 per share); the Committee excluded the two low bidders, advanced seven to management presentations and data-site diligence, and sought non-binding LOIs with markups by July 20, 2016. Six LOIs arrived ($19.20–$24.00; G&W's one day late), and on July 27, 2016 the Committee advanced G&W and Party B to confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation, telling Party C, D, E and F they were out; D and E briefly re-engaged in early August, and Party B reaffirmed its $24.00 on August 4. On August 12, 2016 G&W returned with a $25.00 all-cash LOI (no CVR), Party B declined to raise its $24.00, and the Board determined G&W's offer superior and signed the merger agreement; the deal was announced August 15, 2016. G&W is an operating short-line and regional railroad group, and PWRR's preferred stock converts 100-for-1 into the same $25.00 cash consideration.\"\n\n(1, 1, datetime.datetime(2016, 3, 31, 0, 0), 'Transaction Committee authorized outreach; GHF contacted 11 strategic and 18 financial buyers during the week of 03/28', '25 NDA signers: 11 strategic (incl. Party A, Party B, G&W) and 14 financial; 2 further Class I railroads approached', '05/10/2016 → 05/19/2016', 'Late bids accepted (05/19: nine IOIs received 05/19–06/01)', 'Not final', '9 IOI submitters (unnamed; $17.93–$26.50 per share)', 'Seven advanced to presentations; two low bidders excluded; 16 of 25 signers did not submit')\n(1, 2, datetime.datetime(2016, 5, 27, 0, 0), 'Committee advanced seven to management presentations and data-site diligence; non-binding LOIs with markups due 07/20', '8: seven advanced (5 strategic incl. Party B, G&W, Party E, Party F; 2 financial incl. Party D) + late entrant Party C (strategic)', '07/20/2016', \"Late bids accepted (G&W's LOI arrived 07/21 and was considered)\", 'Not final', '6: Party B $24.00; G&W $21.15 → $22.15; Party E $21.26; Party D $21.00; Party C $19.30; Party F $19.20 (1 strategic + 1 financial did not submit)', 'G&W and Party B advanced to definitive stage; Party C, D, E, F told they were out')\n(1, 3, datetime.datetime(2016, 7, 27, 0, 0), 'Committee advanced G&W and Party B to confirmatory due diligence and negotiations on their higher offers', '2: G&W (strategic), Party B (strategic)', 'none stated', 'No deadline stated', 'Inferred final', '4: G&W $25.00 (08/12); Party B $24.00 reaffirmed (08/04); Party D $24.00 (08/01); Party E $23.81 then $21.26 (08/01–02)', 'signing with G&W on 08/12; Party B, Party D and Party E out')\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport io\\ns = io.open('build.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\\ns = s.replace(\\n \\\"\\\\\\\"Catch-up access: after its 07/12 IOI, Party C was given internet data-site access and a telephone management presentation; the seven earlier bidders had in-person presentations.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"\\\\\\\"Provided late entrant Party C internet data-site access and a telephone management presentation after its 07/12 IOI; the seven earlier bidders had in-person presentations.\\\\\\\"\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\n \\\"\\\\\\\"Revised LOI at $25.00 all cash, dropping the CVR; markups of merger agreement and voting agreement (disclosure-letter markup later); offer to expire 6:00 p.m. 08/13; no financing condition in the executed agreement.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"\\\\\\\"revises #31: $25.00 all cash, dropping the CVR; markups of merger agreement and voting agreement (disclosure-letter markup later); offer to expire 6:00 p.m. 08/13; no financing condition in the executed agreement.\\\\\\\"\\\")\\nio.open('build.py','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('edited')\\nEOF\\npython3 build.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Questions']\\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\\n    print(\\\"=====\\\", r[0], \\\"| words(Q):\\\", len(r[1].split()), \\\"| words(A):\\\", len(r[2].split()))\\n    print(r[1]); print(\\\"REC:\\\", r[2]); print(\\\"WHY:\\\", r[3]); print(\\\"ROWS:\\\", r[4]); print(\\\"CHG:\\\", r[5]); print(\\\"RN:\\\", r[6])\\nws = wb['Deal facts']\\nprint()\\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\\n    print(f\\\"{r[0]!r}  =>  {r[1]!r}\\\")\\nws = wb['Rounds']\\nprint()\\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\\n    print(r)\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825620016,"end":1789825621936}}}}
