{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825655641,"sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","part":{"id":"prt_0b9ec08e8001U7zw4lHVkiNqqR_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f461f2da0ffepmGxMLqn7fNdlL","messageID":"msg_0b9ec08e8001U7zw4lHVkiNqqR","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete: `/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx` — four sheets in order (Deal ledger, Rounds, Questions, Deal facts), 48 events, one process with three rounds. Every quotation was re-verified word-for-word against the filing with its printed page, all controlled columns use the exact required strings, and all date cells are real Excel dates (MM/DD/YYYY), frozen headers, filters on, wrapped, no merges.\n\n## The sale in brief\nProvidence & Worcester (PWRR), a regional freight railroad, began after **Party A**, a Class I rail partner, expressed interest in acquiring equity in Q4 2015. The Board engaged **GHF** (later BMO) in January 2016 and on 03/14/2016 approved soliciting buyers. In the week of 03/28/2016 GHF contacted 29 potential buyers (11 strategic, 18 financial); **25 signed NDAs** (11S/14F) and the Board set a 05/10 IOI deadline, extended to 05/19. Nine IOIs ($17.93–$26.50) drew two low bidders out and seven into management presentations/diligence; a late entrant, **Party C**, joined from early July. Six non-binding LOIs arrived by late July ($19.20–$24.00; **G&W** one day late, then revised $21.15→$22.15; **Party B** top at $24.00 with markups; **Party D**/E/F with diligence conditions). On 07/27 the Committee advanced **G&W and Party B** to confirmatory diligence, dropping C, D, E, F; D and E briefly returned (A$24.00/A$23.81→A$21.26), D withdrew 08/02, B reaffirmed $24.00 on 08/04. On 08/12 **G&W bid $25.00 all cash** (dropping its CVR), B declined to raise, the Board chose G&W and signed; announced 08/15/2016.\n\n## Open Questions (with recommendations)\n- **Q1 – Round map:** 3 rounds (wave+IOIs; seven advanced; G&W/B final stage) vs. a 4th round from the mid-June LOI request (also a 03/24 Round-1 opener, or an 08/04 final-stage boundary). *Recommendation: keep 3 rounds as mapped.*\n- **Q2 – Deadline outcomes:** 05/19 and 07/20 both recorded **Late bids accepted** (IOIs arrived through 06/01; G&W's LOI dated 07/21). *Recommendation: as recorded; Enforced only if all bids are treated as in-deadline.*\n- **Q3 – NDA counts:** the filing's 25 (11+14) vs. Party C's later NDA (and two extra Class I railroads approached); the Board's \"six of the 25 submitted LOIs\" implies C may be inside the 25. *Recommendation: use the stated 25, treat C as additional, base the 16 non-submitters on 25−9=16; screen is Met either way.*\n- **Q4 – Party B's Bid reaffirmed (08/04, $24.00):** kept under C12 (target moved to complete an agreement with B; B's latest priced row sits in a not-final round; B's counsel returned a draft). *Recommendation: keep.*\n- **Q5 – Party E's second exit:** inferred **Dropped by target on 08/04** (continuing set G&W/B named without it) vs. Not selected at signing. *Recommendation: 08/04 drop; this fixes live bidders at signing at two.*\n- **Q6 – Price bases:** LOI prices rested on different transaction-expense / change-in-control assumptions. *Recommendation: record prices as stated, do not adjust.*\n\n## What I could not do\n- Identify Party A, the two additional Class I railroads, the two anonymous low bidders, or the two LOI non-submitters beyond the filing's own words, and fully reconcile the 25-signer count with Party C's NDA (Q3).\n- Date five of the six LOIs other than \"late July\" (sorted to the 07/20 due date per convention) or date the 05/10→05/19 extension more tightly than \"subsequently to 04/27\" (Q2).\n- Record any go-shop, post-signing competing proposal, or G&W financial adviser: the filing reports none, and the post-signing 09/06 BMO-conflict disclosure falls outside the row tests.","time":{"start":1789825648878,"end":1789825655641}}}
